```c
if (same_queue_rq)
    list_del_init(&same_queue_rq->queuelist);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when a request (`same_queue_rq`) is removed from the plug list, the cached request count (`plug->rq_count`) is not decremented. This oversight results in an inaccurate count of requests in the plug structure, which can lead to improper request handling and resource management issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (same_queue_rq) {
    list_del_init(&same_queue_rq->queuelist);
    plug->rq_count--;
}
```
Reason:
The fix adds a decrement operation for the cached request count (`plug->rq_count--`) immediately after removing the request from the plug list. This ensures that the request count accurately reflects the current number of requests in the plug structure, preventing potential issues related to request handling and resource management.

